{"t":"2026-10-22T18:03:00.307Z","event":"finish","launch":"0036-cm-cs","n":1,"role":"cm-cs","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":43022,"cumulative":203086,"cost":0.4,"turns":5,"minutes":0.42,"sessions":[],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I delegated all three orders to `demo-builder`. Each one is now waiting in that builder's queue at the draft stage.\n\n| Order | Lesson | Draft message | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| O-1 | eight-cores-not-eight-times | M-4 | Delegated, waiting at draft |\n| O-2 | faster-link-same-wait | M-5 | Delegated, waiting at draft |\n| O-3 | drivers-stop-switching | M-6 | Delegated, waiting at draft |\n\nThe budget is 150,000 for each order. None of the three waits on another order, so up to three `demo-builder` sessions can work them at the same time.\n\nTwo things confused me:\n1. **Only one builder.** You asked me to split the orders across my builders, but the org has only one builder role, `demo-builder`. It is listed under cm-math and serves both the math and cs lanes. So nothing could be split by role. They only spread out because that role can run three sessions at once.\n2. **Two messages per delegation.** Each delegate call returned two message ids: O-1 got M-1 and M-4, O-2 got M-2 and M-5, O-3 got M-3 and M-6. Only M-4, M-5 and M-6 show in the builder's queue. My guess is that M-1, M-2 and M-3 are the notices about the delegation itself, but I haven't confirmed that."}
