{"t":"2026-10-22T18:06:20.129Z","event":"finish","launch":"0066-demo-builder","n":4,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":86379,"cumulative":1202126,"cost":0.8784,"turns":17,"minutes":3.3,"sessions":["S-3"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"I drafted the claims for LESSON-drivers-stop-switching (order O-3), and it's now with the fact-checker for the plan check. After the hand-in the queue was empty, so the session closed.\n\n- **What I wrote:** only `src/demos/cs/drivers-stop-switching/meta.json`, with status `draft`, the brief fields and 7 claims, all `unverified`. There is no Demo.tsx.\n  - c1 to c5 each make one of the brief's planned claims 1 to 5.\n  - c6 states the stage's road rules (support: convention).\n  - c7 covers the recall question's `why` sentence and names planned claims 2, 4 and 5.\n- **Numbers:** I re-ran the brief's setup in node and got the same results it states:\n  - From all six on B, the meter goes 255 → 210 → 180 → 165, with savings of 45, 30 and 15 minutes.\n  - It ends with 3 drivers on A at 30 min and 3 on B at 40 min.\n  - From all 64 starting arrangements, it takes at most 3 switches, and each switch lowers the meter by exactly the switcher's saving.\n  - When everyone switches at once, it flips between 55 and 60 minutes for ever.\n- **Check:** the draft checker (`claims-draft.mjs`) passed with no findings.\n\nWhat confused me:\n- **Script blocked:** the launcher's guard blocked my first try at the node script, which I'd written with a shell heredoc. I rewrote it as a file with the Write tool and it ran.\n- **Support type:** the brief calls claim 5 \"citation\", but the allowed support types are derivation, simulation, source and convention, so I used `source`.\n- **Interaction label:** the checker doesn't check interaction names. I changed `step-run` to `step-run-button`, which other lessons already use."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:07:25.730Z","event":"start","launch":"0214-demo-builder","n":7,"role":"demo-builder","msgs":["M-23"],"tasks":[],"cwd":"/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/b6-LESSON-eight-cores-not-eight-times","workdirs":["/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/b6-LESSON-eight-cores-not-eight-times"],"tools":["Bash","Read","Write","Edit","Glob","Grep"],"sessionMin":60,"maxTurns":200,"settingSources":["project"]}
