{"t":"2026-10-22T18:50:48.553Z","event":"finish","launch":"0486-chief-of-staff","n":14,"role":"chief-of-staff","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":41976,"cumulative":236987,"cost":0.1999,"turns":6,"minutes":0.56,"sessions":[],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"**ISS-4 (O-2, faster-link-same-wait, parked at launch after a no-go): resumed to build.** The ask is closed and the order is at loop 2 of 4.\n\n- **Why I agreed with the no-go:** I opened the order's accessibility report from QA and it says what the launch record says. The timeline tick labels render at 8.1 px and the \"510 ms\" finish label at 8.9 px. The demo standard's \"on screen means legible\" rule sets a 10 px floor at 390 px wide, so v1 cannot ship.\n- **What I told the builder to change:**\n  - The tick labels and every total label must render at 10 px or more after the SVG scales them.\n  - Text size wins over fit. If the bigger labels push the top of the stage off screen when the reveal opens, cut or fold text the way the demo standard says, and raise any cut teaching sentence with cm-cs.\n  - In the same build, fix the three issues the launch record carries forward:\n    - The caption must change with the state.\n    - The \"(dark)\" send marks must be something the learner can find.\n    - The alt text says \"1 rounds\", which needs fixing.\n  - Bump to v2 with a new Pre-flight v2 section.\n- **Claims stay as they are:** c1–c4 and c6 stay verified and c5 stays withdrawn. Any sentence the builder adds or changes gets a new claim marked unverified.\n\n**What confused me:** the ask says the head of product is the decider and that it routes to me. The launch record also asks the orderer (cm-cs) to resume it. I decided it because the ask is assigned to me and the task told me to."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:51:44.339Z","event":"guard","launch":"0497-demo-builder","n":15,"role":"demo-builder","via":"hook","tool":"Bash","rule":"bash","why":"`<a command the guard cannot read>`: the guard cannot read this line, so it refuses it. To write a file, use the Write tool (not a shell heredoc or redirect); otherwise spell the command out in plain words (no $(…), `…` or variable as a command, git subcommand or script name)","detail":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/demos/cs/faster-link-same-wait/Demo.tsx'\ns=open(p).read()\nrep=[\n(\"\"\"// Geometry: 0-520 ms across 330 px.\nconst X0 = 12;\nconst W = 330;\nconst X = (ms: number) => X0 + (ms / SPAN) * W;\nconst BAR_Y = 34;\nconst BAR_H = 22;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"// Geometry: 0-520 ms across 272 units in a 300-u"}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:53:32.147Z","event":"finish","launch":"0373-fact-checker","n":10,"role":"fact-checker","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":82349,"cumulative":986176,"cost":1.0545,"turns":25,"minutes":7.57,"sessions":["S-9"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I checked three lessons after their build, and all three passed with no claim status changes. The session ended because no more items were queued (3 of the cap of 4 used).\n\n| Item | Lesson | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | O-3 drivers-stop-switching | **pass** → learner |\n| 2 | O-2 faster-link-same-wait | **pass** → learner |\n| 3 | O-1 eight-cores-not-eight-times | **pass** → learner |\n\n- **drivers-stop-switching:** all 7 claims were verified at plan check and haven't changed since. Each one appears where its address says in the kept walkthrough. I re-ran the numbers with my own script: the switch log, the delay meter and the alternating 55/60 rounds all match. The reveal says \"All 64 starts stop within 3 switches\" without the claim's condition that drivers move in turn. It's still true: I tried every possible switching order from all 64 starts and none took more than 3 switches.\n- **faster-link-same-wait:** 5 claims are verified and 1 is withdrawn (the TCP sentence, which is indeed gone from the reveal). The totals 510 / 505 / 110 / 60 match Demo.tsx's own formula, and \"more than eight times faster\" holds (510/60 = 8.5).\n- **eight-cores-not-eight-times:** all 6 claims are verified and unchanged. The stage shows 37.5 / 26.25 / 20.6 / 15 minutes and 1.6 / 2.29 / 2.91 / 4x as claimed. The plan check had asked for 26.25 to show with two decimals, and it does.\n\nEach record is at `company/reviews/<slug>/2026-10-22-fact-check.md` in that order's worktree. I made no edits to any meta.json.\n\nI found two small wording slips in alt text, which aren't factual problems and so didn't block anything: \"1 rounds\" in faster-link-same-wait and \"1 cores\" in eight-cores-not-eight-times.\n\nTwo things were unclear:\n- The pack said to hand in with `next_with` and stop only when told the session is over, but the later items were in other orders' worktrees, not the one this session started in. I wrote each record in its own order's worktree, which is where code would look for it.\n- None of the claims changed status, so the \"row per changed claim\" table in each record just says \"(none)\" and gives the reason."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:54:19.744Z","event":"finish","launch":"0402-learner-evaluator","n":11,"role":"learner-evaluator","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":104784,"cumulative":1059850,"cost":1.013,"turns":24,"minutes":7,"sessions":["S-10"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"The session is over: I reviewed 3 lessons and the queue is now empty. Two passed to launch and one went back to build.\n\n| Item | Outcome | Review file |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. drivers-stop-switching (O-3) | **revise**, back to build | `company/reviews/drivers-stop-switching/2026-10-22-learner-ncm-student.md` |\n| 2. faster-link-same-wait (O-2) | **launch**, on to launch review | `company/reviews/faster-link-same-wait/2026-10-22-learner-packets-only.md` |\n| 3. eight-cores-not-eight-times (O-1) | **launch**, on to launch review | `company/reviews/eight-cores-not-eight-times/2026-10-22-learner-helpers-only.md` |\n\n- **drivers-stop-switching:** the reveal's whole explanation rests on the \"delay meter\", but the lesson never says what the meter adds up. The learner sees 255 and cannot check why it falls by exactly each driver's saving. The reveal also says \"All at once, there was no such meter\", but the meter is on screen during that run, reading 210 and then 255. The fix is to define the meter on the stage, show its values in the all-at-once log, and reword that sentence. There are also some smaller wording and label notes.\n- **faster-link-same-wait:** passes. The list of totals (510 · 505 · 110 · 60) shows the surprise clearly. Non-blocking notes: the stage caption doesn't update when the speed or batch size changes, and the dark \"sending\" marks are hard to see.\n- **eight-cores-not-eight-times:** passes. The bar shows the 15 minutes that cannot be split staying fixed while the rest shrinks, so the learner sees the limit before the reveal names it. Non-blocking notes: the formula uses \"serial share\" and \"parallel share\", which the lesson never defines, and the reveal appears with the stage reset to 1 core.\n\n**What confused me:** the brief named only the drivers-stop-switching worktree, but items 2 and 3 belonged to other orders. I wrote each of their reviews into that order's own worktree under `/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/b6-<task>/`, so each order's commit carries its own review.\n\nI read only the kept walkthroughs and the review template, and committed nothing."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:55:16.591Z","event":"finish","launch":"0432-demo-builder","n":12,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":101513,"cumulative":1495439,"cost":1.2957,"turns":36,"minutes":7.03,"sessions":["S-11"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"**O-3 · LESSON-drivers-stop-switching, build stage (revise round 1).** I handed it in and it went to test1. The pre-run of test1 (`meta.mjs check --order=O-3`) passed and typecheck shows no errors in this lesson. No other item was queued, so the session is over.\n\nI fixed everything the learner review raised and moved the lesson to v2:\n1. **Meter not defined.** The explore hint now defines it: \"for each road, the trip time with 1 car, 2 cars, … : all on B gives 30+35+40+45+50+55 = 255\". A new line under the meter bar shows the current sum, e.g. 10+20+30 + 30+35+40 once the drivers settle.\n2. **Reveal contradicted the stage.** The all-at-once record now reads \"from all on B: 55 → 60 → 55 → 60 min\" with \"meter: 255 → 210 → 255 → 210\" under it. The reveal line is now \"All at once, the meter rose again: nothing stopped the flips (55, 60, 55, 60 min).\"\n3. **Minor fixes.** The button is \"All at once\", without the ×4. \"From all on B\" is shown on the record, and \"your meter\" now reads \"the meter\".\n\n**Trade-off.** To keep the stage at 25 words, I renamed the stage label from \"delay meter\" to \"meter\". The new sum line is numbers only, so it counts no words. The explore hint sits outside the stage and doesn't count either.\n\n**Claims.** c1–c7 are unchanged and keep their verified status. I added c8 (the meter's definition) and c9 (the meter goes 255 → 210 → 255 → 210 when everyone switches at once), both `unverified` for the fact-checker. The v2 pre-flight is in build.md and the v2 changes are in design.md.\n\n**Not checked.** I didn't run reveal-fit locally. The stage is about 1.5 lines taller now (an extra text line in the drawing and a second line in the all-at-once record), so the qa stage is where a fit problem would show up. The reveal is still about 90 words, the same as v1.\n\n**What confused me.** My first edit, a shell heredoc, was refused by the launcher's guard, so I made all the changes with the Edit tool instead."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:56:25.462Z","event":"finish","launch":"0455-head-of-product","n":13,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":114989,"cumulative":1783960,"cost":1.3442,"turns":26,"minutes":7.71,"sessions":["S-12"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I chaired two launch reviews: one lesson is held back, the other goes on to the ship gates. The session ended when the queue ran dry after the second item.\n\n**1. faster-link-same-wait (v1): no-go, so the order is parked.**\n- **Why:** the timeline's labels are too small to read on a phone, which breaks the lesson standard (10 px minimum at 390 px wide) and the brief's own rule (\"labels >= 10 px\"). The QA accessibility report shows 42 instances, across every phase and both themes:\n  - the tick labels 100–500 render at 8.1 px;\n  - the finish label (\"510 ms\", and 505/110/60 in turn) renders at 8.9 px.\n- **Cause:** the design note asked for 10 px, but the picture is scaled down on a phone, which shrinks the text below that.\n- **What still holds:** QA, the fact check (c1–c4 and c6 verified, c5 withdrawn) and the learner review all passed. The findings also ask the builder to fix three smaller notes in the same build:\n  - the stage caption doesn't change with the state;\n  - the dark \"send\" marks are hairlines, too thin to find;\n  - the alt text says \"1 rounds\".\n- **Record:** `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-faster-link-same-wait.md`.\n\n**2. eight-cores-not-eight-times (v1): go, and it moved on to the gates stage.**\n- Every claim is verified, QA passed on phone and desktop, and the learner review says launch. Stage text is 24 words (limit 25) and the reveal about 76 (limit 90).\n- The accessibility report has no text-size findings for this lesson, and the labels measure about 10–11 px on the screenshot.\n- Objections that travel with it:\n  - the three standing ones (no analytics predictions, accessibility review is advisory, learning-designer merged into the builder);\n  - the button labels read \"2/4/8/∞\" instead of the brief's \"2 cores…\";\n  - the reveal's formula uses two terms an intro learner hasn't met;\n  - the stage shows the 1-core state while the reveal talks about 8 cores and unlimited;\n  - the alt text says \"1 cores\".\n- **Record:** `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-eight-cores-not-eight-times.md`.\n\n**What confused me:**\n- **Revise vs no-go:** the brief lists \"revise\" as a launch verdict, but the record must say `go` or `no-go`, and `no-go` always parks the order. There's no way to send a fixable defect back to build without parking it. I wrote no-go and asked the orderer (cm-cs) to resume the first lesson to build. The kernel parked it, even though I left with `--verdict=revise`.\n- **QA passed below the floor:** QA's accessibility check only flags text under 9 px, so a label between 9 and 10 px would pass unflagged. I had to measure the second lesson's labels from the screenshot myself. Its code wasn't on my reading list, so that measurement is approximate."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T18:56:55.256Z","event":"finish","launch":"0497-demo-builder","n":15,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":94401,"cumulative":1575518,"cost":1.1195,"turns":30,"minutes":6.29,"sessions":["S-13"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"I rebuilt LESSON-faster-link-same-wait (O-2) as v2 and handed it in. It has moved on to test1, and the session closed because the queue was empty. I haven't measured the new label sizes myself; the QA stage's accessibility report is the real check. The pre-check that runs test1's command passed, and `npm run check` shows no errors for this lesson. The 811 errors it does report are in other files, such as decision records.\n\n**What changed, against the head-of-product's no-go:**\n- **Label size:** the v1 timeline image was drawn 354 units wide but shown only about 288 px wide on a 390 px phone. That shrank everything to 81%, so tick labels came out at 8.1 px and the total at 8.9 px. v2 draws it 300 × 70 and raises the font sizes (ticks 12, total 13), which should give about 11.5 px and 12.5 px. Nothing was made smaller, and the image is a little shorter than before, so the reveal should still fit on the phone screen.\n- **Caption follows the state:** it now says 1 ms or 0.5 ms per packet when sending one at a time, and \"5 packets take 5 ms\" or \"10 packets take 10 ms\" in the batch states.\n- **Send marks:** the caption calls them \"thin marks\" instead of \"(dark)\", and they are now at least 3 units wide.\n- **Alt text:** it now says \"1 round\", not \"1 rounds\".\n- **Claims:** c1–c4 and c6 stay verified and c5 stays withdrawn, untouched. I added one new claim, c7 (unverified), for the new caption text and alt text. meta.json is now version 2, and `build.md` has a \"Pre-flight v2\" section; `design.md` has a v2 note.\n\n**Things to watch or that confused me:**\n- The stage text is now at exactly 25 words, the most allowed. The busiest frame is the 14-word caption plus \"Totals\" plus the 10 words of button labels, so any further wording change needs a cut somewhere.\n- A launcher guard blocked my first attempt, which used a Python script inside a shell command. I made the edits with the Edit tool instead."}
