{"t":"2026-10-22T19:38:23.911Z","event":"finish","launch":"0651-fact-checker","n":16,"role":"fact-checker","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":61026,"cumulative":652657,"cost":0.7255,"turns":19,"minutes":6.65,"sessions":["S-15"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I checked two lessons this session and passed both. Each now goes to the learner stage. Then the queue was empty, so the session ended.\n\n**1. drivers-stop-switching (version 2): pass**\n- Two claims were new since the plan check, c8 and c9. I checked them with my own simulation and they match.\n  - **c8:** the \"meter\" (total delay) reads 255 with all drivers on road B, 165 with three on each road, and 210 with all on road A.\n  - **c9:** when everyone switches at once, the meter goes 255 → 210 → 255 → 210.\n- The simulation also confirmed c3: all 64 starting arrangements settle within 3 switches, and each switch lowers the meter by exactly what that driver saves.\n- c1–c7 were already verified, and the lesson shows each one where its address says.\n- One small mismatch, not a defect: c2's address quotes a log row like \"driver 2 saves 30 min · meter −30\". The lesson shows the same numbers as a table instead.\n- Record: `company/reviews/drivers-stop-switching/2026-10-22-fact-check-2.md`\n\n**2. faster-link-same-wait (version 2): pass**\n- One claim was new, c7: the model caption and the timeline's alt text. I checked them at every state the walkthrough recorded (start, each button, reset) and against the numbers in the code. They match.\n- c1–c4 and c6 appear in the lesson where their addresses say, and the arithmetic holds.\n- c5 (the TCP sentence) stays withdrawn. It is not in the lesson.\n- Record: `company/reviews/faster-link-same-wait/2026-10-22-fact-check-2.md`\n\n**What confused me:** both lessons already had a `2026-10-22-fact-check.md` from an earlier check. The rules only say what to name a second plan-check record (`-fact-check-plan-2.md`), not a second check record. I named mine `-fact-check-2.md` to match, and code accepted it. I did not open the earlier records, build.md or design.md."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T19:39:20.516Z","event":"finish","launch":"0673-learner-evaluator","n":17,"role":"learner-evaluator","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":86543,"cumulative":810071,"cost":0.7479,"turns":19,"minutes":6.63,"sessions":["S-16"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I reviewed two lessons and gave both a launch verdict. Both orders have moved on to the launch stage, and the session closed because the queue was empty.\n\n1. **drivers-stop-switching (O-3, lesson v2): launch.** The switch log puts each driver's saving next to the meter's drop (45, 30, 15), and that carries the idea. Three small notes, none blocking:\n   - The third answer option asks about driver *orders*, but the reveal answers about the 64 starting *arrangements*. Adding \"in any order\" would close the gap.\n   - After \"All at once\", the picture shows everyone on road A, but the text reads 55 → 60 → 55 → 60. The button doesn't say how many rounds it runs, so I had to work out which state the picture shows.\n   - The lesson shows that the meter works but not why it is built that way.\n   - Review: `company/reviews/drivers-stop-switching/2026-10-22-learner-ncm-student-r2.md`\n\n2. **faster-link-same-wait (O-2, lesson v2): launch.** After \"Double speed\" the timeline looks the same and the total only drops to 505, which shows the surprise before the reveal names it. The list of totals keeps every run side by side. Two small notes:\n   - The 1 ms send marks are barely visible against the grey waits on a phone screen.\n   - Nothing says why a sender waits for a reply, or that real protocols send many packets before waiting.\n   - Review: `company/reviews/faster-link-same-wait/2026-10-22-learner-packets-only-r2.md`, written in that order's own worktree.\n\nThings that confused me:\n- Each order already had an earlier learner review from loop 1, which I didn't open. I wrote new `-r2` files as the template says.\n- `--verdict=pass` on the command line maps to `Verdict: launch` in the review file. The session accepted that.\n- The second item lives in a different worktree from the session's own workdir. I wrote its review there, and the relative `--evidence` path was accepted.\n- On both lessons, the \"Why trust this?\" sheet still shows some claims as not yet checked (c8 and c9 on drivers, c7 on faster-link). That is for the fact-checker, not this stage, but those claims are still open."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T19:40:56.653Z","event":"finish","launch":"0697-head-of-product","n":18,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":116709,"cumulative":1455057,"cost":1.2121,"turns":24,"minutes":7.18,"sessions":["S-17"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I chaired two launch reviews and both lessons got **go**. Both orders now move on to the ship gates. Then the queue was empty and the session closed.\n\n**1. drivers-stop-switching v2 (O-3): go.**\n- **Learner revise fixed:** the meter is now defined on the stage, and the reveal now says the meter \"rose again\" in the all-at-once run, which matches what the stage shows.\n- **Arithmetic:** I re-did it by hand and it agrees with the stage.\n- **Labels:** I measured them from the screenshots at about 11–12 px, above the 10 px floor.\n- **Gates:** all 9 claims are verified, QA passed on phone and desktop, and the learner verdict is launch.\n- **Objections travelling (7):**\n  - No analytics-steward predictions.\n  - Accessibility review is advisory: the a11y report's app and kit items are still open.\n  - The learning-designer is merged into the builder.\n  - Two learner polish notes: option 3 says \"orders\" but the reveal answers with \"starts\", and the \"All at once\" button doesn't say how many rounds it runs.\n  - The kept walkthrough shows c8 and c9 as not yet checked.\n  - The textbook section number (8.3) is unconfirmed.\n- **Record:** `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-drivers-stop-switching.md` in its worktree.\n\n**2. faster-link-same-wait v2 (O-2): go.**\n- **v1 no-go defects fixed:**\n  - The tick labels and the \"510 ms\" total label now render at about 12 px.\n  - The caption follows the state.\n  - The alt text grammar is fixed.\n- **Gates:** c1–c4, c6 and c7 are verified, c5 is withdrawn, QA passed and the learner verdict is launch.\n- **Main objection travelling:** the send marks are still hard to find on a phone. The caption calls them \"thin\" in one state and \"dark\" in another, and the dark ones aren't visible in the screenshot. The learner judged this not blocking.\n- **Other objections:**\n  - The TCP sentence stays cut because the proxy blocks RFC hosts.\n  - No analytics-steward predictions.\n  - Accessibility review is advisory.\n  - The learning-designer is merged into the builder.\n  - The trust sheet in the kept walkthrough shows c7 as not yet checked.\n- **Record:** I overwrote the v1 no-go record at the same path, `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-faster-link-same-wait.md`. Same date and slug, and git keeps v1 at commit 580528507.\n\n**Things that confused me:**\n- **Walkthroughs recorded before the last fact check:** in both lessons the trust sheet showed newer claims as \"NOT YET CHECKED\". I treated this as stale, not a defect, because meta.json shows them verified.\n- **Second item in a different worktree:** the second item's workdir was its own worktree, but the shell kept resetting to the first one, so I used absolute paths.\n- **Label floor not checked by QA:** the a11y report only flags text under 9 px, so I had to measure the 10 px floor by hand from the screenshots."}
